  "track": "track-03",
  "title": "indexes types covering indexes index maintenance and statistics",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "An index is an access structure the optimizer may choose; it is not a promise that a query will use it or that the query will be faster.",
    "A clustered rowstore index defines the leaf-level row organization; a nonclustered index stores key entries and a row locator, with included columns available at the leaf level.",
    "Key order, predicate shape, selectivity, and requested columns determine whether an index can seek, cover, or require lookups. Indexes also add storage, write, logging, and maintenance cost.",
    "Statistics describe data distribution and inform cardinality estimates. Rebuild and reorganize are different operations; neither is an automatic cure for every slow query.",
    "Specialized indexes and SQL Server 2025 preview features have distinct workloads and availability boundaries; identify stable versus preview status and edition limitations."
  ],
